Report a quote left open at the very end of the input.
At end of input, xargs checked for an unmatched quote only if the item
being read had some characters. An opening quote that was the last
byte of the input, as in "a '", started an item with no characters
yet, so it was silently ignored and the command ran with the items
before it.

Treat an open quote at end of input as an unfinished item, which
reports the error.

---
 findutils/xargs.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/findutils/xargs.c
+++ b/findutils/xargs.c
@@ -453,7 +453,8 @@
 	while (1) {
 		int c = getchar();
 		if (c == EOF) {
-			if (p != s)
+			/* An open quote is an error even if nothing follows it */
+			if (p != s || state == QUOTE)
 				goto close_word;
 			goto ret;
 		}
